hadiths[66]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7132","Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that Ghaylan ibn Salamah al-Thaqafi, may Allah be pleased with him, entered Islam while married to ten women. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, commanded him to retain only four. Later, in the caliphate of ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, Ghaylan divorced his wives and distributed his wealth among his sons. When this reached ʿUmar, he rebuked him, suggesting Satan had heard of his impending death and cast the thought into him, and swore that he must take back his wives and wealth, lest ʿUmar grant the wives inheritance regardless and order his grave stoned as the grave of Abu Righal was stoned. > **""Choose four of them.""**"
"7133","ʿAbdullah ibn Masʿud, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, enjoined learning and teaching the Qur'an, knowledge, and especially the laws of inheritance, for he would soon be taken, and knowledge would be withdrawn until two men disputing an inheritance share would find none to inform them. > **""Learn the Qur'an and teach it to the people, learn knowledge and teach it to the people, and learn the fara'id and teach them to the people, for I am one who shall be taken, and knowledge shall be taken until two men differ over an inheritance and find none to inform them.""**"
"7134","Abu Bakrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, commanded learning and teaching the Qur'an and the fara'id, warning that a time would come when two men would dispute an inheritance and find none to judge between them. > **""Learn the Qur'an and teach it to the people, and learn the fara'id and teach them to the people; it is near that there shall come upon people a time when two men dispute over an inheritance and find none to judge between them.""**"
"7135","ʿAbdullah ibn Masʿud, may Allah be pleased with him, said that whoever among them reads the Qur'an should learn the fara'id. If a Bedouin met him and asked whether he recited the Qur'an, and he answered affirmatively, the Bedouin would claim the same; but if then asked whether he knew the fara'id and answered affirmatively, it would be an increase and good, while if he answered negatively, the Bedouin would ask what superiority he then held over him."
"7136","Al-Qasim ibn ʿAbd al-Rahman reports that ʿAbdullah ibn Masʿud, may Allah be pleased with him, said to learn the fara'id, for a man would soon need knowledge he once knew, or remain among a people who did not know it."
"7137","Abu al-Zinad took this epistle from Kharijah ibn Zayd ibn Thabit, from Zayd ibn Thabit, may Allah be pleased with him, to ʿAbdullah, Amir al-Mu'minin Muʿawiyah, may Allah be pleased with him. After praise of Allah, Zayd notes Muʿawiyah's questions on the inheritance of the grandfather, brethren, kalalah, and many judgments whose extent is unknown, and recalls attending such matters with the caliphs after the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, retaining what they willed to retain, and thereafter issuing fatwa on inheritance accordingly to whoever sought it."
"7138","Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, asked for guarantee of six traits in exchange for his guarantee of Paradise. When asked what they were, he mentioned, among them, committing no wrong in dividing inheritances and dealing justly from oneself, then continued the hadith. > **""Guarantee for me six traits and I shall guarantee Paradise for you: do no wrong when dividing your inheritances, and be just from yourselves.""**"
"7139","Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said that what they, the Prophets, leave behind is charity. > **""What we leave is charity.""**"
"7140","ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, reports hearing the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, declare that the ʿasabah of every woman's children belongs to their father, except the sons of Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, for he himself is their ʿasabah and their father. > **""Every woman's children — their ʿasabah belongs to their father — except the sons of Fatimah, for I am their ʿasabah and I am their father.""**"
"7141","Fatimah al-Kubra, may Allah be pleased with her, reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said every woman's children have an ʿasabah to whom they are ascribed, except the children of Fatimah, for he is their guardian and their ʿasabah. > **""Every woman's children have an ʿasabah to whom they belong, except the children of Fatimah, for I am their guardian and I am their ʿasabah.""**"
"7142","ʿAli and Ibn Masʿud, may Allah be pleased with them, said that the ʿasabah of the son of the woman subjected to liʿan is the ʿasabah of his mother."
"7143","Al-Miswar ibn Makhramah and Jabir, may Allah be pleased with them, report that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, ruled that an infant does not inherit until it raises its voice crying at birth, whether by shouting, sneezing, or weeping. > **""The infant does not inherit until he cries out aloud; his crying is that he shouts, or sneezes, or weeps.""**"
"7144","Ibn Sirin reports that Saʿd ibn ʿUbadah, may Allah be pleased with him, divided his wealth among his sons during his lifetime, then died, after which a son was born to him. ʿAmr met Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with them, each confessing sleeplessness over the newborn left with nothing. They went to Qays ibn Saʿd and spoke to him concerning his brother. Qays replied that he would never revoke what Saʿd had concluded, but called them to witness that his own share was for the newborn."
"7145","Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said that the birth-cry of an infant includes sneezing. > **""The istihlal of the infant is sneezing.""**"
"7146","Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, warned of Allah's severe anger upon a woman who introduces into a people one who is not of them, so that he views their privacies and shares in their wealth. > **""Allah's anger is severe upon a woman who brings into a people one who is not of them, who looks upon their private matters and shares with them in their wealth.""**"
"7147","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, ruled that one religious community does not inherit from another. > **""One millah does not inherit from another millah.""**"
"7148","Ibn ʿAbbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that a freedman of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, fell from a palm tree and died, whereupon the Prophet gave his inheritance to the people of his religion."
"7149","Al-Hasan reports that Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, was asked whether the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, had mentioned the matter, and he affirmed, conveying the ruling that Muslims and the People of the Book do not inherit from one another, except that a man may inherit his male or female slave, and that Muslims may marry their women while they may not marry Muslim women. > **""We do not inherit from the People of the Book, nor do they inherit from us, except that a man may inherit his slave or his bondwoman; and we marry their women, but they do not marry our women.""**"
"7150","Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that ʿAqil and Talib inherited Abu Talib, while ʿAli, may Allah be pleased with him, did not inherit him. ʿAli said that for this reason they abandoned their share in the Shiʿb."
"7151","Hassan ibn Bilal reports from Yazid ibn Qatadah that a kinsman of his died outside Islam, and his sister, who shared his religion, inherited him to Yazid's exclusion. Then his father accepted Islam, attended Hunayn with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and died, leaving a slave and date-palms, which Yazid took entirely. His sister then accepted Islam and disputed with him before ʿUthman, may Allah be pleased with him. ʿAbdullah ibn al-Arqam informed that ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, had judged that whoever accepts Islam concerning an inheritance before it is divided receives his share, so ʿUthman judged accordingly. Thus she kept the first inheritance and shared in the second."
"7152","Ibn ʿAbbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, that every inheritance overtaken by Islam before its division is subject to the division of Islam. > **""Every inheritance that Islam overtakes before it is divided is upon the division of Islam.""**"
"7153","Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said there is no orphanhood after puberty. > **""There is no orphanhood after puberty.""**"
"7154","Hanzalah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said orphanhood ends with puberty, and likewise for a girl once she menstruates. > **""There is no orphanhood after puberty, nor orphanhood for a girl once she menstruates.""**"
"7155","ʿUqbah ibn ʿAmir, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that a youth came to the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, saying his mother had died leaving jewelry, asking whether to give it in charity on her behalf. The Prophet asked whether his mother had commanded that, and when he said no, told him to keep his mother's jewelry for himself. > **""Did your mother command you with that? Then keep your mother's jewelry for yourself.""**"
"7156","Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said that wealth left behind belongs to the family, while debt left behind is upon Allah and His Messenger. > **""Whoever leaves wealth, it is for his family; and whoever leaves debt, it is upon Allah and His Messenger.""**"
"7157","Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said that when a people affiliate a man to themselves, he inherits them. > **""No people affiliate a man to themselves except that he inherits them.""**"
"7158","Ibn ʿAbbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, abolished illicit sexual affiliation in Islam. One affiliated through pre-Islamic misconduct to his ʿasabah remains so affiliated, but one who claims a child without lawful basis neither inherits nor is inherited from. > **""There is no musaʿah in Islam; whoever engaged in it in Jahiliyyah has been attached to his ʿasabah; and whoever claims a child without lawful wedlock, he neither inherits nor is inherited from.""**"
"7159","ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, asked the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, about the share of the grandfather. The Prophet expressed astonishment at his question and opined that ʿUmar would die before learning it, and so it was. > **""What is your asking about that, O ʿUmar? I think you will die before you learn that.""**"
"7160","Abu Saʿid, may Allah be pleased with him, said that in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, they used to grant inheritance to him, meaning the grandfather."
"7161","ʿUbadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, said that among the judgments of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, was that the two grandmothers share one-sixth of the inheritance between them."
"7162","Ibn ʿAbbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, said he was the first to reach ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, after he was stabbed. ʿUmar asked him to preserve three things from him, fearing people would not reach him: that he had not judged concerning kalalah, that he was not appointing a successor over the people, and that every slave belonging to him was freed."
"7163","Al-Bara' ibn ʿAzib, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, when asked about kalalah, replied that the summer verse suffices. > **""The summer verse suffices you.""**"
"7164","Samurah ibn Jundab, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that a man came seeking fatwa on kalalah, asking whether a man's kalalah meant brothers through his mother and father. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, answered only by reciting to him the kalalah verse in Surat al-Nisa'. Each time the man repeated his question, the Prophet recited it again, until the man pressed loudly out of eagerness for clarification. The Prophet then swore he would add nothing beyond what he had been given until more was given to him, whereupon the man sat down and fell silent. > **""By Allah, I shall not add for you beyond what I have been given; by Allah, I shall not add for you beyond what I have been given until I am given more concerning it.""**"
"7165","ʿAli, may Allah be pleased with him, was presented with the inheritance case of two paternal cousins, one of whom was also a maternal brother. When told that Ibn Masʿud, may Allah be pleased with him, had given him all the wealth, ʿAli invoked mercy upon him as a jurist, but ruled to first grant him the maternal brother's share, then divide the remainder between the two."
"7166","Zayd ibn Thabit, may Allah be pleased with him, was asked about a husband and a full sister. He gave the husband one-half and the sister one-half. When questioned, he said he had been present when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, judged thus."
"7167","Al-Shaʿbi reports that al-Hajjaj had him brought in bonds. At the palace gate, Yazid ibn Abi Muslim and then Muhammad ibn al-Hajjaj each coached him to disavow himself before the Amir regarding shirk and hypocrisy, as it was no day of intercession. Before al-Hajjaj, when charged with rebellion, al-Shaʿbi answered with an eloquent apology describing straitened dwelling, drought, narrow paths, sleeplessness, fear, and disgrace in which they were neither righteous nor strong, which al-Hajjaj accepted and ordered his release. Later al-Hajjaj needed him on an inheritance case of a mother, sister, and grandfather. Al-Shaʿbi reported five differing Companion views: Ibn ʿAbbas made the grandfather a father, gave the sister nothing and the mother one-third; Ibn Masʿud made it of six, sister three, grandfather two, mother one; the Commander of the Faithful made it thirds; Abu Turab ʿAli made it of six, sister three, mother two, grandfather one; Zayd ibn Thabit made it of seven, mother three, grandfather two, sister two. Al-Hajjaj then ordered the judge to enforce it as the Commander of the Faithful had enforced it."
"7168","ʿAli, may Allah be pleased with him, reports from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, that a man inherits his full brother to the exclusion of his paternal brothers. > **""A man inherits his brother through his father and mother, to the exclusion of his brothers through his father.""**"
"7169","ʿAli, may Allah be pleased with him, said that maternal brothers do not inherit the blood-money of their maternal brother when he is killed."
"7170","Abu Saʿid al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, rode a donkey to Quba' seeking instruction concerning the paternal aunt and maternal aunt, whereupon Allah revealed that there is no inheritance for them."
"7171","Ibn Masʿud, may Allah be pleased with him, said the entire inheritance of the son of the woman subjected to liʿan belongs to his mother."
"7172","ʿAli and Ibn Masʿud, may Allah be pleased with them, said the ʿasabah of the son of the mulaʿanah is the ʿasabah of his mother."
"7173","ʿAdi, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that he was married to two women, one of whom threw a stone and killed the other. He rode to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, at Tabuk to ask about the slain woman. The Prophet ruled that her kin pay her blood-money but do not inherit from her. ʿAdi recalls seeing him upon a red jadʿa' she-camel addressing the people on the three hands and calling to chastity even by bundles of firewood, then raising his hands in witness that he had conveyed. > **""He pays her blood-money but does not inherit from her. O people, hands are three: Allah's Hand is the highest, the giver's hand is the middle, and the beggar's hand is the lowest; so refrain from begging even by bundles of firewood. O Allah, have I conveyed?""**"
"7174","ʿUmar ibn Shaybah ibn Abi Kabir, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that while jesting with his wife his hand struck her and she died during the Tabuk expedition. He informed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, that he had struck her by mistake, and the Prophet ruled that he would not inherit from her. > **""You shall not inherit from her.""**"
"7175","ʿAbdullah ibn ʿAmr, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, judged that blood-money is divided among the heirs of the slain according to their prescribed shares."
"7176","Al-Mughirah ibn Shuʿbah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that Asʿad ibn Zurarah said to ʿUmar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with them, that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, wrote to al-Dahhak ibn Sufyan to grant the wife of Ashyam al-Dababi inheritance from her husband's blood-money."
"7177","Al-Mughirah ibn Shuʿbah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that Zurarah ibn Juzayy said to ʿUmar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with them, that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, wrote to al-Dahhak ibn Sufyan to grant the wife of Ashyam al-Dababi inheritance from her husband's blood-money."
"7178","Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the killing of Ashyam was accidental."
"7179","Ibn ʿAbbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports in marfuʿ form that wala' neither transfers nor shifts. > **""Wala' is neither transferable nor removable.""**"
"7180","Ghaylan ibn Salamah al-Thaqafi, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that Nafiʿ Abu al-Sa'ib had been his slave and fled to the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, during the siege of Ta'if and accepted Islam, whereupon the Messenger freed him. When Ghaylan later accepted Islam, the Messenger returned Nafiʿ's wala' to him."
"7181","ʿAbdullah ibn Abi Awfa, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said wala' is a bond like the bond of lineage. > **""Wala' is a bond like the bond of lineage.""**"
"7182","ʿUmar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, reports hearing the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, say that the wala' is inherited by whoever inherits the wealth, whether father or son. > **""The wala' is inherited by whoever inherits the wealth, whether father or son.""**"
"7183","ʿAli ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, reports from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, that wala' belongs to the one who emancipates. > **""Wala' belongs to the one who emancipates.""**"
"7184","Ibn ʿAbbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said wala' belongs to the one who emancipates. > **""Wala' belongs to the one who emancipates.""**"
"7185","Salma bint Hamzah, may Allah be pleased with her, reports that her freedwoman died leaving a daughter, whereupon the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, granted the daughter one-half and granted Yaʿla, the son of Salma, one-half."
"7186","She further reports that a freedman of hers died leaving his daughter, whereupon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, divided his wealth between her and his daughter, granting her one-half and the daughter one-half."
"7187","Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that a man died leaving his daughter and the patrons who had freed him, whereupon the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, divided his inheritance between his daughter and his patrons."
"7188","Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said whoever aligns himself to other than his patrons has cast off the bond of faith from his neck. > **""Whoever aligns himself to other than his patrons has cast off the bond of faith from his neck.""**"
"7189","Abu Umamah ibn Thaʿlabah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said whoever aligns himself to other than his patrons bears the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people, with neither obligatory nor voluntary deed accepted from him. > **""Whoever aligns himself to other than his patrons, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; Allah accepts from him neither sarf nor ʿadl.""**"
"7190","Jaʿfar ibn Muhammad, from his father, from his grandfather, may Allah be pleased with them, said he found with the hilt of the Messenger of Allah's sword, peace and blessings be upon him, the inscription condemning most severely before Allah the one who kills other than his killer, strikes other than the one who struck him, and denies the favor of his patrons, such a one being quit of what Allah revealed to Muhammad. > **""The most hostile of people toward Allah are the one who kills other than his killer, the one who strikes other than the one who struck him, and whoever denies the favor of his patrons has disavowed what Allah revealed to Muhammad.""**"
"7191","ʿAmr ibn al-ʿAs, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that he came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and said a man had accepted Islam at his hands, possessed wealth, and had died. The Prophet ruled the inheritance for him. > **""Then his inheritance is for you.""**"
"7192","Jabir ibn ʿAbdullah, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that an Ansari man gave his mother a palm-garden for her lifetime. When she died, his brothers claimed equal partnership in it. He refused, they disputed before the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and he divided it among them as inheritance."
"7193","ʿAbdullah ibn ʿAmr, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that a man said he had given his mother a garden during her life, she had died leaving no heir besides him. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, replied that Allah had returned his garden to him and accepted his charity. > **""Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has returned your garden to you and accepted your charity.""**"
"7194","Sinan ibn Maslamah reports that a Muhajir man gave his mother a large land as charity. She died leaving no heir besides him. He asked the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, what to do with it, describing his mother's beloved station. The Prophet replied that Allah had secured his reward and returned his land, to do with as he wished. > **""Allah has made your reward binding and returned your land to you; do with it as you wish.""**"
"7195","ʿUbadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that a man devoted all he owned except his horse as charity. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, took his land and placed it among the needy. His parents then came complaining of destitution and circling with the needy, asking for sustenance from their son's charity. The Prophet returned it to them. When they died, their son who had given it inherited it back, and asked whether it was lawful for him, and the Prophet told him yes, to eat it with wholesome enjoyment."
"7196","Bishr ibn Muhammad ibn ʿAbdullah ibn Zayd, whose father conveyed the call to prayer, reports that ʿAbdullah ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, gave in charity his sole sustaining property and handed it to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him. His father complained that it was their livelihood. The Messenger summoned ʿAbdullah and announced that Allah had accepted his charity and returned it as inheritance upon his parents, and Bishr said they thereafter inherited it among themselves."
"7197","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that an Ansari man devoted all his wealth as charity. His parents became destitute and sat with the needy, then complained to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, that their wealthy son's charity had impoverished them. The Prophet returned the son's charity upon them. When they died, he sent to their son ordering restoration of the charity, for charity is neither inherited nor granted as life-tenancy. > **""Your son's charity is returned upon you both. Return the charity, for charity is neither inherited nor granted as ʿumra.""**"
